  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 100 PM MDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nWednesday should be the coolest day of this week, with max temps in \nthe mid to upper 80s. We should continue to see an uptick in the \nafternoon and shower activity. A weak disturbance should brush the \nregion adding a bit of lift to the area. The best chance of storms \nthis day will likely be across the southern Sangres and extending \neastward across the CO/NM border. The central mtns may actually dry \nout some this day as drier air moves in from the northwest. Storms \nmay linger well into the evening hours over the plains this day.\n\nThursday, ridging build once again over the region and noticeably \ndrier air advects in the from the northwest. Any showers and storms \nthis day will likely be over the far southeast plains. Temps will \nwarm up a tad, with mainly mid to upper 80s over the plains and \nvalleys. \n\nFriday...zonal flow aloft. Main precip chances will likely be over \nthe CONTDVD region with only isolated activity elsewhere. 90s return \nto the plains with mid 80s valleys. \n\nWeekend into early next week, statistical guidance starts to show \nvariability in the temps, as the guidance products solutions start to \ndisagree on how the pattern develops. This variability is quite \napparent  during the early week time period as temps show a very \nlarge range. Overall pops chances increase somewhat so we may see a \nbetter chance of precip during this period. Looking at the CPC 6-10 \nday guidance leans wetter over the region with a bit above normal \ntemps. Based on this, gridds show upper 80s plain SAT, cooling to \nU70s/L80s plains by MON, with pop chances gradually increasing each \nday. \\/Hodanish",
